UID:filmfonds-wildcards-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212445Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260707
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260708
SUMMARY:Deadline: Filmfonds Wildcards (Documentary\, Fiction\, Animation)
DESCRIPTION:Talent prize for recently graduated bachelor filmmakers from a 
 Dutch film or art academy (documentary\, fiction or animation). Winners re
 ceive a small development purse to start a new short film\, and a much lar
 ger realisation budget once they have a producer attached. Annual round\; 
 deadline 7 July 2026 at 17:00.\n\nOrganisation: Nederlands Filmfonds\nLoca
 tion: Netherlands\nAward: Up to €3\,000 development to the maker + up to
  €50\,000 realisation (paid via attached producer)\nDuration: One-off ta
 lent prize per round\n\nMore: https://www.filmfonds.nl/subsidies/subsidie/
 filmfonds-wildcards-documentaire-fictie-en-animatie?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.filmfonds.nl/subsidies/subsidie/filmfonds-wildcards-documen
 taire-fictie-en-animatie?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
LOCATION:Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rtm-pitch-iffr-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212445Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: RTM Pitch 2026 (IFFR)
DESCRIPTION:Eighth edition of RTM Pitch\, IFFR's open call for Rotterdam fi
 lm talent. Submit a plan for a film between 5 and 20 minutes long\; a jury
  of film experts and IFFR programmers selects one filmmaker to receive EUR
  25\,000 to realise the film (with coaching and an IFFR 2028 premiere) and
  a runner-up to receive a EUR 5\,000 development budget co-funded by QISSA
 . All filmmakers are welcome\; this edition especially encourages genre fi
 lms (horror\, science fiction\, thriller\, fantasy) that use genre convent
 ions for a distinctive personal vision. Submit a written film plan (story\
 , setting\, team\, budget and financing\, cinematography vision\, with opt
 ional supporting material) or a video pitch of no more than three minutes 
 (Vimeo or YouTube link) via the application form. Deadline: Sunday 30 Augu
 st 2026\, 23:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: International Film Festival Rotterd
 am (IFFR)\nLocation: Rotterdam\, Netherlands\nAward: EUR 25\,000 for the w
 inner (EUR 20\,000 from the City of Rotterdam\, EUR 5\,000 from VEVAM Fond
 s) to realise the film\, plus tailored coaching and an IFFR premiere\; a r
 unner-up receives a EUR 5\,000 development budget co-funded by QISSA. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: Short film of 5 to 20 minutes\; winning film pr
 emieres during RTM Day at IFFR 2028\n\nMore: https://iffr.com/en/blog-rtm-
 pitch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iffr.com/en/blog-rtm-pitch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotterdam\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iffr-darkroom-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212445Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Darkroom 2027: Work-in-Progress Showcase (IFFR Pro)
DESCRIPTION:Darkroom is IFFR's work-in-progress platform\, running during C
 ineMart\, where recently completed or nearly finished films are launched t
 o the international film industry. Selected teams present an excerpt of th
 eir work to international sales agents\, festival programmers\, buyers and
  other industry professionals in a closed presentation\, and receive tailo
 red mentorship matched to the project's needs from senior editors\, market
 ing strategists\, festival experts and distribution professionals. All Dar
 kroom projects get a curated agenda of one-to-one meetings with potential 
 creative and business partners plus facilitated informal networking\, and 
 IFFR Pro awards are handed out to projects from the selection. ELIGIBILITY
 : the project must have been supported by IFFR through at least one of the
  following: new for 2027\, the filmmaker has been selected for the Tiger C
 ompetition or Bright Future programme at IFFR within the last 10 years\; t
 he project has been supported by the Hubert Bals Fund through any of its f
 unding schemes\; the project was formerly presented at BoostNL\; the proje
 ct was formerly presented at CineMart\; or the project's main producer or 
 main co-producer has been a Rotterdam Lab participant. In addition\, the p
 roject must have no sales agent attached\, Darkroom must be its first work
 -in-progress showcase\, and it must not have a confirmed world or internat
 ional premiere at the time of application (if that changes after selection
  at a winter festival\, applicants must tell the Darkroom team immediately
  so eligibility can be rechecked). Projects that do not meet all criteria 
 are ineligible. Recent editions selected 6 to 12 projects. Deadline 1 Octo
 ber 2026\, 22:00 UTC. Free to submit.\n\nOrganisation: International Film 
 Festival Rotterdam (IFFR)\nLocation: Rotterdam\, Netherlands. Presentation
 s take place during CineMart at IFFR 2027 (28 January to 7 February 2027).
  Open internationally: eligibility is defined by the project's prior conne
 ction to IFFR\, not by the applicant's country.\nAward: No participation f
 ee and no fee to submit. Selected projects compete for the IFFR Pro awards
  attached to Darkroom: the Eurimages Outreach Award of EUR 30\,000 (shared
  with Lightroom)\, the HBF Empowerment Award of EUR 10\,000\, the Filmmore
  Work-in-progress Post-production Award of EUR 5\,000\, and the 4DR Studio
 s Award (an in-kind studio or workshop prize\, shared with CineMart). Part
 icipation also includes tailored mentorship\, a closed industry presentati
 on and a curated agenda of one-to-one meetings. Award line-up is per the m
 ost recent published edition and may change for 2027.\nDuration: Work-in-p
 rogress showcase during CineMart at IFFR 2027\, 28 January to 7 February 2
 027\n\nMore: https://iffr.com/en/iffr-pro/darkroom?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iffr.com/en/iffr-pro/darkroom?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotterdam\, Netherlands. Presentations take place during CineMart 
 at IFFR 2027 (28 January to 7 February 2027). Open internationally: eligib
 ility is defined by the project's prior connection to IFFR\, not by the ap
 plicant's country.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:filmfonds-netherlands-film-production-incentive-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212445Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Film Production Incentive (October 2026 round
 )
DESCRIPTION:The Netherlands Film Production Incentive is the Film Fund's au
 tomatic cash rebate for feature films\, animated films and documentaries\,
  returning up to 35 percent of qualifying Dutch production costs. It is de
 signed to keep production spend in the Netherlands and is assessed on a po
 ints system rather than artistic panel review. WHO CAN APPLY: only Dutch p
 roducers representing independent production companies. The company must b
 e legally registered in the Netherlands (including Bonaire\, Sint Eustatiu
 s and Saba) for at least two years\, operate continuously in film or audio
 visual production\, and be represented by a producer who has produced at l
 east one majority film with a budget of EUR 500\,000 or more that had a Du
 tch cinema release. PROJECT THRESHOLDS: feature films and animated films n
 eed a minimum production budget of EUR 1 million and at least EUR 150\,000
  in qualifying costs\; documentaries need a minimum budget of EUR 250\,000
  and at least EUR 100\,000 in qualifying costs. FURTHER CONDITIONS: a guar
 anteed Dutch cinema release with a minimum 12-week window\, at least 50 pe
 rcent of the budget unconditionally promised in writing by third parties\,
  at least two unaffiliated financiers\, and a minimum score of 75 points o
 n the automatic assessment system. Deadline 26 October 2026 at 17:00 CET.\
 n\nOrganisation: Netherlands Film Fund (Nederlands Filmfonds)\nLocation: N
 etherlands. Applicant production companies must be legally registered in t
 he Netherlands\, including Bonaire\, Sint Eustatius and Saba.\nAward: Cash
  rebate of up to 35 percent of qualifying Dutch production costs\, capped 
 at EUR 3 million per year per applicant production company. The annual bud
 get is EUR 20 million divided across four rounds at roughly EUR 5 million 
 per round\, with an extra EUR 3 million in the first round. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Per-project production incentive\, applied for per round\
 n\nMore: https://www.filmfonds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-product
 ion-incentive?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.filmfonds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-production-in
 centive?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Applicant production companies must be legally regist
 ered in the Netherlands\, including Bonaire\, Sint Eustatius and Saba.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:filmfonds-production-incentive-high-end-series-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T212445Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Film Production Incentive: High-End Series (O
 ctober 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The High-End Series strand of the Netherlands Film Production I
 ncentive extends the Film Fund's 35 percent cash rebate to high-end drama\
 , documentary and animated television series\, returning up to 35 percent 
 of qualifying Dutch production costs. WHO CAN APPLY: independent productio
 n companies based for at least two years in the Netherlands\, an EU member
  state\, the EEA or Switzerland\, producing audiovisual content on a conti
 nuing basis\, and represented by a producer who has produced either a majo
 rity film with a minimum budget of EUR 500\,000 and a Dutch cinema release
 \, or a majority television series in the same category. Note that despite
  the broader basing rule\, only applicants from the Netherlands\, Bonaire\
 , Sint Eustatius and Saba may actually apply. PROJECT THRESHOLDS: minimum 
 production budget per broadcast minute varies by category\, at EUR 4\,000 
 for documentary and EUR 8\,000 to EUR 12\,000 for drama and animation. FUR
 THER CONDITIONS: at least 50 percent of the production budget secured in w
 riting from third parties\, a guaranteed television or VOD broadcast in th
 e Netherlands (or in two or more countries for co-productions)\, and a min
 imum score of 75 points on the automatic assessment system. Deadline 26 Oc
 tober 2026 at 17:00 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Netherlands Film Fund (Nederland
 s Filmfonds)\nLocation: Netherlands. Only applicants from the Netherlands\
 , Bonaire\, Sint Eustatius and Saba may apply.\nAward: Cash rebate of up t
 o 35 percent of qualifying Dutch production costs\, capped at EUR 3 millio
 n per project per year per applicant production company. The 2026 annual b
 udget is EUR 9.5 million across three rounds\, plus an additional EUR 0.4 
 million in the first round carried over from 2025. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Per-project production incentive\, applied for per round\n\nMore: 
 https://www.filmfonds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-production-incen
 tive-high-end-series?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
URL:https://www.filmfonds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-production-in
 centive-high-end-series?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Only applicants from the Netherlands\, Bonaire\, Sint
  Eustatius and Saba may apply.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
